            <h3>🧬 Biology</h3>
 
            <p>
                Malunggay is a small tree with a branching growth
                form. Its leaves are compound and consist of many
                small leaflets. The plant produces fragrant flowers
                that are generally white to yellowish, sometimes
                with a reddish or crimson tinge.
            </p>
 
            <div class="science-facts">
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Growth Rate</strong>
                    <span>
                        Moringa is a relatively fast-growing
                        multipurpose tree under suitable
                        environmental conditions.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Mature Height</strong>
                    <span>
                        It can reach several metres in height.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Root System</strong>
                    <span>
                        It develops a substantial root system
                        that supports the plant and allows it
                        to obtain water and nutrients from the soil.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Leaf Structure</strong>
                    <span>
                        Leaves are compound and contain numerous
                        small leaflets.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Bark</strong>
                    <span>
                        The bark is generally whitish to
                        grayish in appearance.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Flowering / Fruiting</strong>
                    <span>
                        Moringa produces fragrant flowers and
                        elongated fruits containing seeds.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
            </div>
 
        </div>

 
        <!-- ECOLOGY -->
 
        <div class="science-info-card">
 
            <h3>🌎 Ecology</h3>
 
            <p>
                Moringa is native to South Asia but has been
                introduced and cultivated in many tropical and
                subtropical regions. It is associated with
                seasonally dry tropical environments.
            </p>
 
            <div class="science-facts">
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Habitat</strong>
                    <span>
                        Seasonally dry tropical environments,
                        woodland, savanna, shrubland, and
                        cultivated areas.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Soil Requirements</strong>
                    <span>
                        Can grow in a variety of soils when
                        suitable drainage and growing conditions
                        are available.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Water Requirements</strong>
                    <span>
                        Can tolerate relatively dry conditions
                        once established, but adequate water
                        supports healthy growth.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Sunlight</strong>
                    <span>
                        Grows well in warm areas with sufficient
                        sunlight.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Native Range</strong>
                    <span>
                        Northeastern Pakistan to Northwestern India.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
                <div>
                    <strong>Wildlife Interactions</strong>
                    <span>
                        Its flowers and plant structure can
                        interact with insects and other organisms
                        in the surrounding ecosystem.
                    </span>
                </div>
 
            </div>
 
        </div>

 
        <!-- ENVIRONMENTAL BENEFITS -->
 
        <div class="science-info-card">
 
            <h3>🌱 Environmental Benefits</h3>
 
            <div class="benefit-grid">
 
                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <span>🌬️</span>
 
                    <h4>Carbon Sequestration</h4>
 
                    <p>
                        Moringa removes carbon dioxide from the
                        atmosphere through photosynthesis and
                        stores carbon in its growing biomass.
                    </p>
 
                </div>

 
                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <span>💨</span>
 
                    <h4>Oxygen Production</h4>
 
                    <p>
                        Oxygen is released during photosynthesis
                        while the plant produces organic compounds
                        needed for growth.
                    </p>
 
                </div>

 
                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <span>💧</span>
 
                    <h4>Watershed Protection</h4>
 
                    <p>
                        Vegetation contributes to the protection
                        of soil and water within vegetated
                        landscapes.
                    </p>
 
                </div>

 
                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <span>🌱</span>
 
                    <h4>Erosion Control</h4>
 
                    <p>
                        Plant roots and vegetation can help
                        stabilize soil and reduce exposure
                        of bare soil to erosion.
                    </p>
 
                </div>

 
                <div class="benefit-item">
                    <span>🦋</span>
 
                    <h4>Biodiversity</h4>
 
                    <p>
                        Moringa can contribute plant structure
                        and biological resources to the surrounding
                        ecosystem.
                    </p>
 
                </div>
 
            </div>
 
        </div>

 
        <!-- PHOTOSYNTHESIS -->
 
        <div class="science-info-card photosynthesis-card">
 
            <h3>☀️ Photosynthesis & Climate</h3>
 
            <p>
                Moringa leaves carry out photosynthesis using
                sunlight, carbon dioxide, and water. The process
                produces organic compounds that support plant
                growth, while oxygen is released as a by-product.
            </p>
 
            <div class="photosynthesis-flow">
 
                <div>
